content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-114 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-20500, raw-water transfer line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: the reported 8.3 mm/s at the drive-end bearing housing exceeds the 7.1 mm/s RMS Zone C/Zone D boundary and falls within Figure 3's Zone D range of 7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS. The applicable HF-300 bearing-housing criterion classifies this as 'Damage likely — stop the pump'; SSP-07 additionally requires immediate stopping for the manufacturer's highest severity zone and notification of the reliability engineer before restart. Figure 3 is specifically an RMS measurement, so confirmation of the report's measurement method is listed under open questions without delaying the stop action.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing temperature: 70 C is exactly at, and therefore still within, the manual's 'Normal up to 70 C' limit. It is 10 C below the 80 C alarm and 20 C below the 90 C trip. The manual specifies housing-surface temperature measurement. Because 70 C is not above the manufacturer's alarm limit, SSP-07's temperature-based requirement to raise a priority-1 work order within the shift is not triggered; the urgent response instead arises from the Zone D vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Leakage: no leakage is reported. No numerical leak-rate limit is supplied. The manual's leakage-at-shaft-seal troubleshooting path, which includes mechanical-seal replacement, is therefore not supported by this report, and seal replacement is not included as a response to vibration alone.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "1. Misalignment — the first manual-listed probable cause of high vibration; check alignment before condemning components. The report contains no alignment measurement to confirm or exclude it.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "2. Bearing wear — a manual-listed probable cause of high vibration. The drive-end measurement location warrants particular inspection of the drive-end bearing, but the normal-limit housing temperature does not by itself diagnose bearing wear.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "3. Impeller imbalance or damage — a manual-listed probable cause requiring impeller inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "4. Cavitation — a manual-listed probable cause; check NPSH. The report provides no suction-condition or NPSH evidence with which to confirm it.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Immediately stop P-114 and keep it out of service while the Zone D condition is addressed. Notify the reliability engineer before any restart, as required for vibration in the manufacturer's highest severity zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before any work inside the pump or on its seal, electrically isolate and apply lock-out/tag-out at the MCC; mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves; drain and vent the pump; and obtain the required line-break permit.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check alignment in accordance with manual section 5.4 and review/check NPSH. Verify whether the reported 8.3 mm/s value was RMS and preserve the measurement details for the reliability engineer.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If rotating-assembly removal is needed for inspection, use the HF-300 back pull-out arrangement, which allows removal without disturbing the casing or pipework. The assembly weighs 68 kg, so use the signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment specified in the safety controls.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the bearings and impeller for the manual-listed high-vibration causes. If inspection establishes that bearing-pair replacement is required, install drive-end bearing HF3-512 (6312-C3) and non-drive-end bearing HF3-510 (6310-C3). On reassembly, for any corresponding fasteners disturbed, use Table 5 with lightly oiled threads: M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm and M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C11",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out method does not itself require opening the casing. If the casing is separately opened, replace casing gasket HF3-120 and tighten the M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm with lightly oiled threads.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Where the alignment check identifies misalignment, perform laser alignment after the mechanical corrective work. Record the alignment and inspection findings; the supplied evidence does not provide an alignment tolerance.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before any permitted restart, maintain the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry. Notify the reliability engineer before restart. When vibration measurement is next performed, measure both bearing housings, classify the highest reading using Figure 3, and continue the manual's weekly condition-monitoring regime; also record housing-surface temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Quantity is one; stage conditionally and use only if inspection establishes that the standard bearing-pair replacement is required.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Quantity is one; stage conditionally as the other bearing in the standard bearing-pair replacement, not as an automatic diagnosis from the vibration reading.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket. Quantity is one only if the casing is opened; the manual requires replacement whenever the casing is opened. It is not inherently required for back pull-out removal alone.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Highest-severity-zone vibration control: stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Internal-pump/seal-work control: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit, with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Lifting control for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly: because it exceeds SSP-07's 25 kg threshold, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment. The manual also explicitly requires lifting equipment for this assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal operating control: maintain Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing replacement: the standard allowance for replacing the bearing pair is 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, to be used only if inspection confirms that this repair is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional laser alignment: the standard allowance is 1.5 hours with 1 technician if laser alignment is performed following the alignment check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, differs from the manual's parts list and Table 5: for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above it requires cartridge seal HF3-450B, no sleeve measurement, and 30 Nm gland-nut torque, whereas the manual lists component seal HF3-450 and 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts on lightly oiled threads. P-114 is serial HF3-20500, which is below HF3-22000, so the bulletin expressly directs this asset to continue using HF3-450 and manual Table 5. Therefore, if seal work is separately authorised later, HF3-450 and 25 Nm apply; HF3-450B, its 30 Nm torque, and its pre-set/no-sleeve-measurement instruction do not apply under this bulletin. No seal replacement is presently included because no leakage was reported.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Confirm that the reported 8.3 mm/s value is vibration velocity RMS and obtain any existing non-drive-end bearing-housing reading. Figure 3 is calibrated in mm/s RMS, and the manual calls for measurements on both housings with classification of the highest reading. Do not operate the stopped pump merely to fill these data gaps without following the Zone D restart-notification requirement. (C06, C07, C15)",
    "Record the alignment, bearing and impeller inspection, and NPSH findings. The current evidence cannot select among the manual-listed causes or establish that either bearing, the impeller, or any other part actually requires replacement; the listed bearings are therefore conditional. (C09)",
    "Obtain the applicable alignment acceptance tolerance and the available/required NPSH data. The supplied chunks require an alignment check and an NPSH check but provide neither an alignment tolerance nor numerical NPSH criteria, so no quantitative acceptance judgement can yet be made. (C09)",
    "The evidence gives standard labour only for mechanical-seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement and laser alignment. It does not provide durations for diagnosis, isolation, removal, inspection or reassembly, so a total job duration has not been estimated. (C12)",
    "Confirm the site's administrative priority mapping for Zone D vibration if required. SSP-07 explicitly prescribes a priority-1 work order for temperature above the manufacturer's alarm limit, which 70 C does not meet, while separately mandating an immediate stop for highest-zone vibration. P1 has been selected here to action that immediate-stop condition, not because the temperature alarm was exceeded. (C02, C07, C15)",
    "The supplied documents require reliability-engineer notification before restart but do not state a numerical post-repair restart acceptance reading or any additional engineering approval criterion. Confirm the restart acceptance requirements with the reliability engineer rather than inventing a threshold. (C07, C15)"
  ]
}
